    en: "This unit introduces K1 children to the ideas of family, friendship, belonging, care, and everyday relationships through a non-language curriculum lens.\n\nThe unit should feel warm, familiar, and highly accessible. Children at this stage are still settling into classroom life and group routines, so the non-language lessons should help them connect school experience with people they know, daily care, shared play, and simple social understanding.\n\nRather than trying to mirror the Power Up language unit too closely, the non-language unit should build a parallel early-years experience around:\n\n- people who care for us;\n- friends we meet at school;\n- families and homes;\n- being kind, safe, and included;\n- everyday classroom belonging.\n\nThe overall aim is not academic intensity. The aim is meaningful participation through hands-on, age-appropriate, emotionally secure experiences.",
